Spec: Device-authorized FRP backend

Purpose:
  Preserve actual authenticated device/application authority across pinned FRP control, work, visitor and hole-punching paths.

Owns:
  ./README.md
  ./authority.patch
  ./prepare.py
  ./verify.ps1
  ./build-android.ps1

Structure:
  ./overlays: Additional narrowly scoped backend implementation and actual path verification.

References:
  /control-plane/authority/transport_gate.sdd
  /docs/adr/0002-frp-authorization-boundary.md
  /docs/adr/0015-authenticated-transport-control.md

Must:
  Build only an ignored derived copy of the fixed upstream commit; leave shared upstream source and installed runtimes untouched.
  Keep legacy listeners distinct from the new mode; new mode accepts actual standard mTLS Agent scope and never falls back to shared-token or empty-identity admission.
  Bind backend work and visitor sockets to their actual authenticated control subject, including application and role, rather than trusting RunID alone.
  Enforce current authorization on actual hole-punch visitor/client/report paths as well as precheck, and close active relay flows on cancellation.
  Keep the Agent data mTLS and local grant boundary necessary even after transport admission succeeds.
  Require actual patched-backend tests before claiming backend authorization or direct-connect acceptance.
  Keep Agent STUN contacts explicit and separate from legacy public defaults, preserving real same-socket multi-destination observation rather than inventing mapping samples.
  Derive portable relative module references and omit temporary checkout VCS metadata from packaged binaries; generated source-copy paths are not runtime configuration.
  Preserve active owned XTCP carriers across individual open cancellation and stale hole-punch completion; new attempts must not tear down unrelated business streams.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify authenticated FRP control/work/publication/relay paths on pinned source.
  [x] #2 Verify actual hole-punch scope binding, bypass rejection and revocation.
  [ ] #3 Connect platform-owned private runtime bridges and verify independent business flows.
